Live dashboard: API serves UI + inference posts live data

- Installed FastAPI + uvicorn[standard] into the venv.
- app.py: CORS (LAN/file:// origins), mount web/ as static (dashboard + theme
  served from the API), new POST /api/v1/alerts so the inference-side rule engine
  can push fired alerts to the store the dashboard reads.
- run_cpu.py: --api-url flag; POSTs 5s zone-states (UC-29) and every alert
  (R-01/02/03/05/06) to the API, best-effort (never blocks inference). Fixed a
  variable shadow (capacity `cap` clobbered the VideoCapture handle).
- services/__init__.py so `services.api.app` imports as a package.
- scripts/demo.sh: one-command live demo (API + inference), open
  http://localhost:8000/web/dashboard.html
- Verified end-to-end on the synthetic clip: zone cards go AMBER, alert feed
  shows R-06 CRITICAL intrusion + R-01, occupancy report renders. 84 tests green.

